Expose, after two themes by Mark Whittaker (phob1an), GNU General Public
License (LICENSE):

  Expose Dark, a KDE Plasma window decoration, version 1.1
  https://store.kde.org/p/2347990

  Expose Dark, a Kvantum theme, version 2602
  https://store.kde.org/p/2348069

  Expose Air Dark, a Kvantum theme, version 2605a
  https://store.kde.org/p/2357405

art/ holds their artwork and settings as they were published. The window
decorator and control look here are written for Renku and Haiku, with colours
and sizes measured from that artwork, and the buttons and check marks taken from
it by tools/make-expose-art.py.

These add-ons are under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later, unlike the rest of Power
Theme, which is under the MIT licence. Power Theme doesn't link them: app_server
and applications load them, like any other decorator and control look.

Expose Dark's Kvantum theme has no dark palette, so the dark theme's controls come
from Expose Air Dark instead.

Not ported: the decoration's soft shadow, which a decorator can't blend with
what's behind a window, and the rounded corners' anti-aliasing, for the same
reason; the window buttons' hover state, which decorators don't get; the Kvantum
themes' tabs anywhere but along the top, which are Haiku's; and Expose Dark's wider
scroll bars, because Haiku's windows lay themselves out around its usual width.
